Capability sentinel for the pro-down-workflow probe.

The probe executes committed fixtures under testdata/workflows/pro-down
through the real Ptah CLI. It proves the bare `atlas migrate down`
revision-format default decided in stokaro/ptah#810: `atlas migrate apply`
records Atlas-format revision rows on a real SQLite database, and a bare
`atlas migrate down` — no `--revision-format` flag — must read exactly
those rows, execute the embedded txtar down bodies, and clear the revision
history (before #810 the bare verb read Ptah's native revision table and
silently rolled back nothing). Atlas keeps `migrate down` in its
proprietary Pro build, so these fixtures are intentionally separate from
the Atlas schema round-trip corpus (stokaro/ptah#758).
